================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI GDPRExportPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing idle/loading/notFound/
unavailable/error/loaded over an injectable GDPRExportDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web
GDPRExportArtifact 1:1 (production binds OperatorConfidenceStore.gdprExport(id:) through the seam). The
page reproduces the web chrome (title/subtitle), the 503 subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the
artifact-id lookup panel (text field + Look-up button + hint, Enter-to-submit), the pre-lookup empty
state, the 404 not-found banner, the four artifact stat cards (Status GlassPanel + Format / Size / Storage,
adaptive grid), the artifact-details panel (id + SHA-256 mono with copy buttons, user, and created/
completed/expires absolute+relative timestamps), the export-failed banner, and the download panel (hint +
Download button when complete, status-specific caption otherwise), using the P2 tokens + P3 shared
components (no hand-rolled glass). The web's 10s queued/running poll is reproduced by pollWhilePending().
Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (31 keys added); display
formatting (formatBytes/formatDateTime/formatRelative) is ported and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms
by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0, previews included), an executed model harness
(36/36), and a route-logic harness (35/35). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to one pre-existing,
out-of-scope feature-views preview type-inference timeout (forbidden to commit-fix), with ZERO diagnostics
in any of my files and a clean whole-module type-check.

